        "A soil element divides into solids, water and air. The void ratio e is void volume over solids volume; porosity n is void volume over total volume, with e = n/(1 - n). Water content w is the mass of water over the mass of solids, times 100. These phase relations convert every field or laboratory measurement into the numbers {S} design needs.",
        "Atterberg limits describe fine soils by water content: the liquid limit where the soil flows, the plastic limit where it crumbles, and their difference, the plasticity index. A high PI warns of compressible, moisture-sensitive clay. Casagrande's chart plots PI against liquid limit to classify soils, giving engineers of {S} a shared vocabulary before any test pit is dug.",
